      "content": [
        {
          "title": "A01: Broken Access Control & A02: Cryptographic Failures",
          "body": "### 1. Broken Access Control Prevention\nNever rely solely on client-side role checks. Every API endpoint must enforce server-side tenant isolation:\n\n```go\n// ✅ SECURE: Verify that the requested resource belongs to the authenticated user\nfunc GetAccountHandler(c *gin.Context) {\n    userID := c.GetString(\"auth_user_id\") // Extracted from verified JWT\n    accountID := c.Param(\"id\")\n    \n    var account Account\n    if err := db.Where(\"id = ? AND user_id = ?\", accountID, userID).First(&account).Error; err != nil {\n        c.JSON(404, gin.H{\"error\": \"Account not found or access denied\"})\n        return\n    }\n    c.JSON(200, account)\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Cryptographic Standards:\n- **Passwords**: Never use MD5 or SHA-256. Use **bcrypt** (work factor >= 12) or **Argon2id**.\n- **Data at Rest**: Use **AES-256-GCM** with authenticated data (AEAD)."
        },
        {
          "title": "A03: Injection & Parameterized Query Enforcement",
          "body": "<div class=\"my-6 p-5 bg-slate-900 rounded-2xl border border-slate-800 shadow-lg text-white\">\n  <div class=\"flex items-center justify-between pb-3 mb-3 border-b border-slate-800 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-300\">\n    <div class=\"flex items-center space-x-2\">\n      <span class=\"w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-blue-500\"></span>\n      <span class=\"uppercase tracking-wider font-mono\">OWASP Top 10 Multi-Layered Defense-in-Depth Model</span>\n    </div>\n    <span class=\"text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-500 font-normal\">AEON SYE Technical Blueprint</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"w-full overflow-x-auto\">\n    <svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 190\" class=\"w-full h-auto min-w-[650px]\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n      <defs>\n        <linearGradient id=\"blueGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n          <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#3b82f6\" />\n          <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#1d4ed8\" />\n        </linearGradient>\n        <linearGradient id=\"emeraldGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n          <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#10b981\" />\n          <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#047857\" />\n        </linearGradient>\n        <linearGradient id=\"purpleGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n          <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#8b5cf6\" />\n          <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#6d28d9\" />\n        </linearGradient>\n        <linearGradient id=\"amberGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n          <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#f59e0b\" />\n          <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#b45309\" />\n        </linearGradient>\n        <linearGradient id=\"roseGrad\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\">\n          <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#f43f5e\" />\n          <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#be123c\" />\n        </linearGradient>\n        <filter id=\"shadow\" x=\"-5%\" y=\"-5%\" width=\"110%\" height=\"115%\">\n          <feDropShadow dx=\"0\" dy=\"4\" stdDeviation=\"4\" flood-color=\"#000\" flood-opacity=\"0.3\"/>\n        </filter>\n      </defs>\n      \n      <!-- Outer Layer: WAF -->\n      <rect x=\"30\" y=\"20\" width=\"740\" height=\"150\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"#0f172a\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\" />\n      <text x=\"50\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold font-mono uppercase\">Layer 1: Perimeter &amp; WAF Defense (Rate Limiting, DDoS, IP Whitelist)</text>\n\n      <!-- Middle Layer: App Gateway & Input Sanitization -->\n      <rect x=\"60\" y=\"55\" width=\"680\" height=\"100\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#1e293b\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\" />\n      <text x=\"80\" y=\"80\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold font-mono uppercase\">Layer 2: Application Security (Strict Schema Validation, Parameterized SQL, CSRF Token)</text>\n\n      <!-- Inner Layer: Cryptography & Secrets -->\n      <rect x=\"90\" y=\"90\" width=\"620\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"url(#emeraldGrad)\" />\n      <text x=\"400\" y=\"120\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Layer 3: AES-GCM-256 Data Encryption &amp; HashiCorp Vault Secrets</text>\n    \n    </svg>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\nSQL Injection remains the #1 cause of catastrophic data leaks. Dynamic string concatenation in database queries is strictly prohibited.\n\n```go\n// ❌ VULNERABLE TO SQL INJECTION:\nquery := fmt.Sprintf(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = '%s' AND password = '%s'\", inputUser, inputPass)\ndb.Raw(query)\n\n// ✅ SECURE: Parameterized query ensures input is treated strictly as data, never code\ndb.Where(\"username = ? AND status = ?\", inputUser, \"Active\").First(&user)\n```\n\nFor NoSQL and GraphQL engines, always enforce input type schemas and maximum query depth limits."
        },
        {
          "title": "A10: Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) & Defensive Headers",
          "body": "SSRF occurs when an application fetches a remote resource without validating the user-supplied URL (e.g. hitting AWS metadata or internal K8s services).\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ SECURE URL VALIDATION: Whitelist trusted domains and block internal IP ranges\nfunction isSafeUrl(targetUrl: string): boolean {\n    const parsed = new URL(targetUrl);\n    const blockedHosts = ['10.', '192.168.', '172.16.', '127.0.0.1', 'localhost', '169.254.169.254'];\n    \n    if (parsed.protocol !== 'https:') return false;\n    return !blockedHosts.some(blocked => parsed.hostname.startsWith(blocked));\n}\n```\n\n### Mandatory HTTP Security Headers:\n- `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'`\n- `X-Frame-Options: DENY`\n- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`\n- `Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains`"
        }
      ],
